cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below, and cite the original model of
  Lee, Iwasa, Dieckmann and Sigmund (2019) listed under references.
title: >-
  Who guards the guardians when the guardians rotate? Umpire rotation and inherited
  integrity in an evolutionary model of institutional corruption
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Aziz
    given-names: Mohammad Ari Alexander
    affiliation: >-
      School of Electrical Engineering and Informatics, Institut Teknologi Bandung,
      Indonesia
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-10"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - corruption
  - evolutionary game theory
  - institutions
  - term limits
  - replicator dynamics
  - bifurcation
abstract: >-
  Reproduction of the institutional corruption model of Lee, Iwasa, Dieckmann and
  Sigmund (PNAS 2019), verified against its SI Appendix, and an extension with
  term-limited umpires whose newcomers may inherit the integrity of incumbents.
  Includes mean-field analysis, individual-based simulations, a rare-exploration
  Markov chain, all numeric results and a draft paper.
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: Joung-Hun
      - family-names: Iwasa
        given-names: Yoh
      - family-names: Dieckmann
        given-names: Ulf
      - family-names: Sigmund
        given-names: Karl
    title: Social evolution leads to persistent corruption
    journal: Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences
    year: 2019
    volume: 116
    issue: 27
    start: 13276
    end: 13281
    doi: 10.1073/pnas.1900078116
